From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob McSwain <jacob@mcswain.dev>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:12:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): a long poll no longer holds a restart stop

gateway.restart_reads_grace_seconds (0 = off): with restart_listener_handover, dashboard requests still running when a restart stop seals the listener get that many seconds instead of 5, and the ones cancelled after it get that long to unwind instead of until their worker thread returns. A long poll in a worker thread (the device plugin's request bus waits up to 25 s) held every idle stop 15 to 23 s, and with it every request the stop holds for the next gateway.
---
 gateway/config.py                         |  7 +-
 gateway/config_loader.py                  |  1 +
 gateway/run_api.py                        | 18 ++++-
 gateway/run_shutdown.py                   |  9 ++-
 tests/gateway/test_restart_reads_grace.py | 81 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 111 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/gateway/test_restart_reads_grace.py

